## Conclusion

Both target behaviors verified bidirectionally — each pin FAILS when its
load-bearing term is removed (naming the exact test + the wrong value), PASSES
when restored. The k-scaling term proved load-bearing for three of the four pins
(decoupling, exact-pair, floor); the coincident-0 pin falls out of the total
primitive independently. No pin is vacuous.
